{
 "note": "Extended capacity-law sweep: nine widths x the domain's alpha grid x 5 seeds, one job per (domain, width) so the runner's slots are used. Fixes two defects of the four-width fit: the exponent's two-dof interval, and HAR's grid stopping short of the healthy branch (rel_scatter 0.686 at its smallest alpha). The old grids are subsets of the new ones, so the two runs remain comparable. This manifest lists the 18 cells whose results ship (battery/har at m in {16,24,32,48,64,96,128,192,256}); the campaign also defined nine RadioML cells on the same nine widths, which returned after this release was cut and are not used, because they run at 60 epochs against the 25-epoch RadioML protocol of configs/jobs_E2c*.json. RadioML's capacity numbers therefore come from the four-width E2c sweeps in repro/results/E2c/, which ship.",
